{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro","kind":"prose","text":"mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro\"></a><p>At the boundary between the single-baryon mass tower and the electroweak and nuclear sectors, the categorical Higgs mechanism, the interface-knot Markov parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code>, and the weak-sector Plancherel normalization close the spectral completeness conditions of the six-term formula.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-mass-theory-orphan-reconnect-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":48,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":38,"unknown":0,"stale":17},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
